    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.jump2d\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.x\n\n### Description\n\nWhen plugins add a highlight with a priority greater than 999, and that highlight is not cleared(ie has content), mini.jump2d is unable to dim.\n\nExamples:\n1. An Oil buffer with a minihues colorscheme: The files can be [dimmed](https://github.com/stevearc/oil.nvim/blob/b73018b75affd13fa38e2fc94ef753b465f770d7/lua/oil/init.lua#L903), the directories however can not. See video.\n2. A MiniFiles buffer with a minihues colorscheme: Both directories and files cannot be dimmed.\n3. A MiniFiles buffer with the 'thorn' colorscheme: See example 1, because 'thorn' does not [define](https://github.com/jpwol/thorn.nvim/blob/e7074d253db38d76c5b709ac29f22c5e508da9d3/lua/thorn/groups/mini.lua#L21) the corresponding MiniFiles highlights. Thus, [MiniFilesFile](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/6664ea9af6c43dc31934e27476bbe61c556c8dc1/lua/mini/files.lua#L1401) is cleared by the mini.files plugin, and can be dimmed.\n4. A buffer with colorcodes highlighted with mini.hipatterns. Characters in the pattern cannot be dimmed.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Create separate 'nvim-repro' config directory:\n    - '~/.config/nvim-repro/' on Unix\n    - '~/AppData/Local/nvim-repro/' on Windows\n\n2. Inside 'nvim-repro' directory create a file named 'init.lua'.\n   Populate it with the following content:\n\n```lua\nvim.pack.add({ 'https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim' })\nvim.cmd.colorscheme('minispring')\n\nvim.pack.add({ 'https://github.com/stevearc/oil.nvim' })\nrequire('oil').setup()\n\nlocal jump2d = require('mini.jump2d')\njump2d.setup({\n  mappings = { start_jumping = '' },\n  view = { dim = true, n_steps_ahead = 2 },\n})\nvim.keymap.set({ 'n', 'x', 'o' }, 'sj', function() MiniJump2d.start(MiniJump2d.builtin_opts.single_character) end)\n\n```\n\n3. Run `NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro nvim` (i.e. execute `nvim` with `NVIM_APPNAME` environment variable set to \"nvim-repro\").\n   Wait for all dependencies to install.\n\n4. Repro\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d35d8895-dcae-411f-8c94-a79f45d01e89\n\n- Open neovim in the neovim repository\n- Type `:Oil` and enter\n- Type `sj` and `d`\n- Notice that filenames are dimmed, but directories are not",
