            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> The behavior that no explicit extmark priority means very high priority is unfortunate, but it is what it is\n\nVery unfortunate. Consequently, there will be a number of scenario's where mini.jump2d's dim is not working as expected. I just tested snacks.explorer, same outcome as Oil. \n\n> So all in all, I think this is 'stevearc/oil.nvim' and 'mini.files' issues, not 'mini.jump2d'. Do you have time to make a PR for 'mini.files'?\n\nYes, certainly",
